{
    "background_story": "Kayden was a marine biologist with a passion for studying the Sparidae family of fish. Growing up near the coast, he spent countless hours exploring the tide pools and coral reefs, fascinated by the diverse species of porgies and sea bream. As he delved deeper into his research, Kayden became particularly interested in the unique characteristics of the Sparidae family, such as their distinctive teeth and feeding habits. His dedication paid off when he discovered a new species of Sparidae in the depths of the Mediterranean. Kayden's groundbreaking research earned him international recognition, and he was hailed as a leading expert in his field. He continued to explore the ocean's secrets, always driven by his love for the Sparidae family and the mysteries they held.",
